[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2730082952","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104273#issuecomment-2730082952","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104273","id":2730082952,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iucKI","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-17T16:08:00Z","updated_at":"2025-03-17T16:54:15Z","body":"> The compiler does not fully understand the meaning of the code\r\n\r\nGenerally I would also favour just using the builtin library ABS just so it can use the most appropriate technique for the platform (which might be a SIMD function).\r\n\r\nOf course the gold standard is to profile / do benchmarks for the two approaches on different platforms / compilers, I don't know how much ABS is a bottleneck for us. Note that sometimes library funcs have to cope with really obscure cases to match \"the standard\" (e.g. NaN, infinity, denormals, signed zero) which we might not properly handle or be too worried about.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https:/